  "prefLabel": "Csp 405.01 New Hampshire Scholar Designation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Csp 405.01 New Hampshire Scholar Designation. Eligible students who are determined by their awarding postsecondary institution to be on track to receive a New Hampshire scholar designation in the second semester of their senior year of high school shall be considered to have earned the New Hampshire scholar designation for purposes of a scholarship award. If an eligible student who is awarded a scholarship of $2,000.00 per year fails to earn the New Hampshire scholar designation, that student’s scholarship shall be reduced to $1,000.00 per year.\n\nSource. #13144, eff 12-9-20 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Csp 400); ss by #13302, eff 12-10-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/csp100-700.html"
